.TH TANDEM 1 "2026-08-12" "tandem 4.2" "User commands"
.SH NAME
tandem \- runs Windows programs, Android apps and Linux packages
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tandem
.RI [ command ]
.RI [ argument ]
.br
.B tandem-exe
.I file.exe
.br
.B tandem-apk
.I file.apk
.br
.B tandem-appimage
.I file.AppImage
.br
.B tandem-jar
.I file.jar
.br
.B tandem-deb
.I file.deb
.br
.B tandem-rpm
.I file.rpm
.br
.B tandem-flatpak
.I file.flatpakref
.br
.B tandem-snap
.I file.snap
.br
.B tandem-script
.I file.sh
.br
.B tandem-android
.br
.B tandem-repair
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Tandem
makes
.IR .exe ,
.IR .msi ,
.IR .apk ,
.IR .xapk ,
.I .AppImage
and
.I .jar
files open with a double click on Linux. It does not replace Wine or Waydroid:
it is a layer of decision, translation and diagnosis on top of them.
.PP
For Windows programs, Tandem runs the file, reads Wine's error output looking
for missing libraries, translates each one into the
.BR winetricks (1)
package that provides it, installs, and tries again. It is the loop an
experienced person would do by hand.
.PP
For Android apps, Tandem inspects the package before installing it
(architecture, minimum system version, and whether it is split into parts) and
reports incompatibilities in a sentence, instead of failing with no
explanation.
.PP
For the formats Linux itself uses, the diagnosis comes before the run. An
.I .AppImage
is checked for a complete download, the right kind of processor, and the
execute permission the browser did not give it; when FUSE is missing, Tandem
opens the program by unpacking it rather than failing, and puts the program in
the applications menu using the shortcut the AppImage itself carries. A
.I .jar
is read to find out whether it is a program or merely a piece of one, and which
version of Java it needs \(em so that
.RB \(lq "class file version 65" \(rq
is answered with \(lqthis needs Java 21\(rq.
.PP
For the distribution's own packages, the whole diagnosis happens
.B before
the password is asked for. That is not a preference, it is a measured fact:
.B apt-get install -s
answers with no privilege at all and already says which dependency cannot be
satisfied. A
.I .deb
built for another version of the system is reported as exactly that, instead of
as \(lqlibssl1.1 but it is not installable\(rq \(em and the difference between
that case and \(lqa repository you need to add is missing\(rq is decided by the
name: a library with its version welded into its name will never install here.
.PP
An
.I .rpm
does not install on this system and Tandem does not offer to convert it: a
converted package carries dependency names that do not exist here and skips the
install scripts, producing something that looks installed and is not. Instead,
Tandem looks for the same program in the machine's own repositories and shows
the command.
.PP
A
.I .sh
is the one case where Tandem's default answer is
.B not
to run. A script can do anything its owner can do, and the difference between a
vendor installer \(em makeself, a payload behind a shell header \(em and any
old script decides what is offered first: run it, or read it. That is why
.I application/x-shellscript
is the only type
.B tandem repair
deliberately does
.B not
claim: opening a downloaded script in a text editor is a better answer than
running it, and Tandem does not take a type away from somebody who is already
doing the right thing.
.B tandem-script
stays reachable through \(lqOpen with\(rq and through
.BR "tandem install" .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B tandem
Opens the graphical panel. With no graphical session, shows this help.
.TP
.BI "tandem install " file
Installs or runs the file, choosing between the nine formats by type. When the
name says nothing, it decides by content, always from the most specific mark to
the most generic: every AppImage is an ELF, every
.I .jar
is a zip, and every
.I .deb
is an
.B ar
archive.
.TP
.B tandem android
Opens the Android screen.
.TP
.B "tandem preparar"
Installs what is missing \(em Wine, winetricks, 32-bit support, adb, Java, FUSE
and Android (Waydroid) \(em and starts Android up. Flatpak is left out on
purpose: it is installed on the spot, if a
.I .flatpakref
turns up. Asks for the password once only. This cannot happen during the
package install:
.BR dpkg (1)
holds a lock while
.I postinst
runs, and an
.BR apt-get (8)
in there would wait forever.
.TP
.BI "tandem programas " [name]
Lists the installed Windows programs and opens the chosen one, without
depending on the system menu. Under Wayland, GNOME only re-reads the
application list after logging out and back in, so a freshly installed program
does not exist for the user until the next login.
.TP
.BI "tandem desinstalar " [name]
Removes a Windows program and clears up the shortcuts left pointing at
nothing. It only works in Tandem's own profile: uninstalling changes the
profile, and somebody else's profile is untouchable.
.TP
.B tandem doctor
Shows the diagnosis of the environment: Wine version, 32- and 64-bit support,
Waydroid state and protected profiles. It says what EXISTS.
.TP
.B tandem autoteste
Exercises Tandem on this machine and says what WORKS \(em which is not the same
question. An installed piece may not work: it has happened that
.BR zenity (1)
was present and still refused every accented text, erasing the entire interface
without leaving a trace. The self-test runs each thing for real and looks at
the result; where it cannot exercise something, it says it skipped rather than
pretending it passed.
.TP
.BI "tandem alternativas " name
Looks for a Linux program that does the job of a Windows program. It separates
what IS the same program with an official Linux version from what merely does
something similar, always saying what changes.
.TP
.BI "tandem receita " file
Writes to standard output what Tandem has learnt about a program, as text that
fits in a message and can be checked before being sent. To keep it in a file,
redirect:
.IP
.EX
tandem receita ~/Downloads/system.exe > recipe.txt
.EE
.IP
The recipe comes out marked with where its confidence came from: a lesson the
owner confirmed on screen is worth something different from one where the
program merely exited without an error.
.TP
.BI "tandem receita --importar " "recipe program"
Uses somebody else's recipe. The recipe is refused if it does not declare
itself as one, if it is for another program, or if it carries a component name
with an unexpected character \(em it becomes an argument to
.BR winetricks (1),
and input from outside cannot carry a command.
.TP
.BI "tandem memoria " [name]
Shows what Tandem has learnt about each program: which components fixed it,
which did not, whether it opened, and how long it took.
.IP
The
.B I checked
line is what Tandem verified for itself, as opposed to what you told it. After
installing a missing component it looks on disk for the file the program asked
for, in a width the program can actually load, and records one of four answers:
the file arrived, it arrived built for the other processor width, it is still
missing, or there was nothing it could check for. The last of those is not the
same as \(lqnothing was wrong\(rq, and it says so.
.IP
A lesson where Tandem proved the file arrived but nobody confirmed the program
itself works is worth more than a silent run and less than your word. If you
share it \(em as a recipe or with the community list \(em it goes out labelled
.BR entregue ,
and the list counts it as half a report.
.TP
.BI "tandem esquecer " name
Erases what it learnt about a program. Next time it works it out again.
.IP
.B tandem esquecer enviados
erases something different: the record this machine keeps of the lines it has
sent to the community list. That record exists so you can answer "what has this
machine sent about my shop?" without trusting anybody's word for it, which also
means it has to be yours to delete. Erasing it changes nothing at the other end
\(em what is sent is sent.
.TP
.B tandem repair
Reapplies the file associations. Use it when a double click opens the
\(lqOpen with…\(rq dialog instead of Tandem.
.TP
.B tandem dados
Shows the files
.I you
created inside Windows \(em documents, spreadsheets, program databases \(em
separated from the environment, which Tandem knows how to rebuild on its own.
.RS
.TP
.B tandem dados salvar
Copies only those files into a
.I .tar.gz
in the home folder. It is quick and small, because it does not take the
environment along.
.TP
.BI "tandem dados restaurar " [copy]
Puts the files back from a copy. Nothing that already exists is overwritten;
only the missing files go in. With no argument, it uses the most recent copy.
.RE
.TP
.BI "tandem backup " [where]
Saves Tandem's Windows environment into a file. With no argument it goes to the
home folder; give a folder or a file name and it goes there instead, which is
how you put it on a pen drive. It includes your files, but it is heavy; to take
only the data, use
.BR "tandem dados salvar" .
.TP
.BI "tandem restore " [file]
Restores the Windows environment. With no argument it uses the most recent
backup in the home folder; name a file and it uses that one. The archive is
read before anything is replaced, so a backup that did not arrive whole is
refused with your environment untouched.
.TP
.BI "tandem tema " [which]
Appearance of Tandem's own windows: \fBsistema\fR follows the computer and is
the default, \fBescuro\fR is Tandem's own dark look. Nothing else on the
computer changes.
.TP
.BI "tandem protect " path
Marks a Wine profile as untouchable. Tandem never installs or changes anything
inside a protected profile.
.TP
.BI "tandem idioma " [code]
With no argument, shows which language Tandem is speaking and the list of the
ones that exist. With a code
.RB ( en ", " pt_BR ", " es ", " fr ", " zh_CN ", " hi ", " ar ),
switches to it and remembers the choice.
.IP
Tandem does not ask about the language during the package install: it follows
the language Linux is already set to, and says which one it picked the first
time it runs. Translations not yet checked by somebody who speaks the language
as their first are marked with an asterisk on the list, and Tandem says so
outright to whoever picks one.
.IP
English is the default. That is what an unrecognised locale gets, and it is
what every catalogue falls back to when a key is missing.
.TP
.B tandem identidade
Shows, side by side, everything a program can read about this computer when it
ties a licence to it, and says where each thing comes from: from your real
machine, from a fixed value every Wine in the world answers identically, or
from inside the Windows environment. It is read-only: it does not start Wine,
does not ask for a password and changes nothing. It exists to answer the
question that comes up when a program asks to be activated again with nothing
having changed.
.TP
.B tandem portas
Lists which COM or LPT port each device plugged into the machine will appear on
for Windows programs \(em pinpad, scale, printer, barcode scanner in serial
mode. It warns about the two cases that break this silently: the device that
landed on a port above COM4, which a lot of old shop software refuses, and the
missing
.B dialout
group, without which the device shows up on the list and will not open.
.IP
A run of kernel serial lines with no UART behind them is collapsed into one
line that says what they are. A modern PC registers thirty-two of them and has
none: that is measured, not assumed, and it is what pushes a real USB adapter
up to COM33.
.TP
.BI "tandem portas fixar " "port path"
Pins a device to a port of your choosing, for example
.BR "tandem portas fixar COM2 /dev/ttyACM0" ,
so that a Windows program can both see the port in its settings and actually
open it \(em a printer or pinpad on the wrong port is the usual reason nothing
prints. It only works in an environment created by Tandem.
.BR "tandem portas soltar " port
undoes it, handing the port back to Wine.
.TP
.BI "tandem servico instalar " "folder"
Sets up a web service \(em a program that runs and must stay running \(em from a
folder, and keeps it alive. Tandem looks at the folder to work out what it is
(Node, Python, PHP, a Java
.IR .jar ,
a plain program, a shell script, or a Windows server
.I .exe
under Wine), writes a per-user
.B systemd
service for it, starts it, tries to make it survive a reboot, and tells you the
address to open. No administrator rights and nothing under
.IR /etc .
Add
.BI "--porta " N
to say which port it answers on, and
.BI "--comando " \(dq...\(dq
to give the start command yourself when the folder does not make it obvious.
.IP
.B tandem servico
on its own says, for each service, whether it is running, whether anything is
listening on its port, and whether it actually answers \(em in plain words.
.BR "tandem servico iniciar" ,
.BR parar ,
.BR reiniciar ,
.B remover
and
.B abrir
are the rest;
.B "tandem servico registros " name
shows what a service printed. A Windows
.I .exe
service is only ever run in an environment Tandem created (rule 1).
.TP
.B tandem lista
Shows the community list: what has already worked on other people's machines,
per program.
.TP
.B tandem lista atualizar
Downloads the list now. It is a public text file, fetched over HTTPS \(em the
model of an ad blocker's filter lists. Nothing from this machine is sent, and
nothing is installed: the list becomes a suggestion, and Tandem goes on asking.
.IP
Tandem also fetches it on its own, at most once a day, in the background, the
first time it meets a Windows program it knows nothing about. That direction
only ever DOWNLOADS \(em it is the half of the list that costs the shop nothing
\(em and it never delays a double click, which is why a fetch started now helps
from the next run rather than this one.
.TP
.B tandem lista desligar
Stops the automatic download.
.B tandem lista ligar
turns it back on. Either way,
.B tandem lista
says which of the two is in force.
.TP
.B tandem versao
Says which Tandem this is. Tandem also checks once a day, in the background,
whether a newer one has been published, and tells you once when there is.
.IP
It never installs it, and that is deliberate rather than unfinished: a program
that can replace itself from the internet hands whoever controls that address
every machine running it, and a shop counter is not the place to take that
trade for the convenience. The notice carries the address; updating stays
something you do, with a command you can read and a checksum you can check.
.IP
.B tandem versao nao-avisar
stops the notice;
.B tandem versao avisar
turns it back on.
.TP
.BI "tandem contribuir " program
Assembles the standard line with what this Tandem has learnt and shows it in
full, for you to check and send if you want. Tandem never sends on its own.
The line carries no file name, folder, user name, machine name, network address
or log; the generator refuses to produce it if any of those turns up. The
format is described in
.IR docs/LIST\-FORMAT.md .
.TP
.BR "tandem enviar " [ sim | nao ]
Turns automatic sending of what Tandem learns to the community list on or off.
With no argument, shows the state, how many lines are held in the queue, and
where they would go.
.PP
It is born
.B on.
That is a reversal, and the reason is the measurement below: born off, the list
was empty. The owner is TOLD rather than asked \(em by
.BR dpkg (1)
at install, and again the first time there is a real line to send, with that
line displayed in full. Turning it off is one command,
.BR "tandem enviar nao" ,
and it is named in both notices.
.PP
What makes a default defensible rather than merely convenient is not the
default: it is that the record CANNOT carry anything personal. No file name, no
folder, no user name, no machine name, no network address, no line of log \(em
and the sieve that guarantees it runs twice, once when the line is built and
once at the moment of sending.
.PP
Why this exists: up to version 3.8 the list only ever came down, and the
consequence was measurable \(em it was
.BR empty .
The way to contribute was to read a line on screen, copy it, open a browser,
create an account on an unfamiliar site and paste it into a form. Nobody does
that, and the empty list is the measure of how many did.
.PP
What goes out is one line of eight fields per program, the same one
.B tandem contribuir
shows. The sieve that guarantees it carries no file name, folder, user name,
machine name or network address runs
.B twice:
when the line is assembled and again at the moment of sending \(em because the
queue is a text file, and a text file is exactly what somebody edits by hand.
.PP
None of this delays a double click: sending happens in the background, at most
20 lines a day, and a machine with no internet keeps the line and forgets about
it.
.TP
.B tandem socorro
Gathers into a single file everything somebody needs to help you at a distance:
diagnosis, self-test, what Tandem has learnt, and the technical logs. The file
shows file paths from this machine \(em check it before sending.
.TP
.B tandem logs
Shows the most recent technical log.
.TP
.B tandem version
Shows the installed version.
.TP
.B tandem help
Shows the list of commands. With no graphical session, it is what
.B tandem
on its own does.
.SH PROTECTED PREFIXES
A Wine prefix Tandem did not create is always treated as read-only by the
automation: the program is run inside it, what is missing is reported, and
nothing is installed. This exists so that a production system that already
works is never changed by accident.
.PP
Prefixes created by Tandem carry the file
.I .tandem-prefixo
at their root. The explicit list of
.B tandem protect
takes precedence over that marker.
.SH EVIDENCE
.B doctor
and
.B autoteste
answer different questions, and the difference has already cost this project
dearly. Listing that a piece is installed is weak evidence: it proves the piece
exists, not that it works. Five defects found in the field were invisible to a
list and visible to an exercise \(em among them the error window that never
opened and the progress bar that brought the whole program down. Before
trusting that something works here, exercise it.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/tandem/wine
Default Wine prefix, created on first use.
.TP
.I ~/.config/tandem/protegidos.txt
Wine profiles the automation may never modify, one per line.
.TP
.I ~/.config/tandem/idioma
The language the owner chose, if they chose one.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/tandem/*.log
Technical logs for each command.
.TP
.I ~/.config/mimeapps.list
File associations applied by
.BR "tandem repair" .
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/tandem/memoria/
What Tandem has learnt about each program, one file per program, indexed by a
fingerprint of the file.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/tandem/wine/.tandem-verbos
Receipt of the components already installed in that profile. It stops an
install that has already been paid for from being repeated.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/applications/tandem-appimage-*.desktop
Menu shortcuts Tandem created for AppImages, with the
.I X-Tandem-AppImage
line pointing at the file. A shortcut whose file has disappeared is deleted on
its own at the next listing.
.TP
.I ~/.config/tandem/tipos-aplicados.txt
The file types Tandem has already claimed on this machine. On an upgrade, only
the types absent from this list are claimed again \(em a type the owner never
saw Tandem take over carries no decision of theirs to overwrite.
.TP
.I ~/.config/tandem/.primeira-vez
Which version of Tandem did the first-run work. It used to be an empty file,
and that is why an upgraded machine never claimed the new formats.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/tandem/lista.tsv
The community list, when downloaded by
.BR "tandem lista atualizar" .
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/tandem/traducao-suspeita.tsv
Components Tandem installed that did not deliver the file that was asked for
\(em that is, a mapping error of its own.
.TP
.I ~/tandem-dados-*.tar.gz
Copies of your files, made by
.B tandem dados salvar
and automatically before any destructive operation.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TANDEM_LIB
Where to look for the libraries. Default:
.IR /usr/lib/tandem .
It exists so the test suite can exercise the executables without installing the
package.
.TP
.B TANDEM_IDIOMA_FORCADO
Forces the language for one run, ahead of the owner's choice and the system
locale.
.TP
.B TANDEM_PREFIXO_PADRAO
Wine profile used for standalone programs. Default:
.IR ~/.local/share/tandem/wine .
.TP
.B TANDEM_LISTA_URL
Where to download the community list from.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
No error path ends in silence. When there is a graphical session, errors appear
in a window and a notification; without one, they go to the terminal. In either
case they are recorded in the log, reachable with
.BR "tandem logs" .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wine (1),
.BR winetricks (1),
.BR waydroid (1),
.BR adb (1)
